From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] Match Fenix's toolbar, URL editing and home page, on Firefox 154 and 158

Toolbar: one Fenix toolbar (FenixToolbar.sys.mjs, toolbar.css) instead of
the desktop nav bar plus tab strip, with Fenix's URL pill, page progress bar
on the edge facing the page, URL fade only when the text overflows, and the
private colour scheme in private windows.

URL editing: a full-window awesomebar. With the toolbar at the bottom the
results are listed bottom-up and Up/Down follow what is on screen. On 154,
whose URL bar is a permanent breakout popover, will-change on the URL bar
made it the containing block of the fixed results (height 0): turn it off
while editing and place the bar and results against the window. The tab
tray and the dialog layer are manual popovers too, so the top-layer URL
bar is no longer drawn over them. Placeholder "Search or enter address".

Home: about:fenixhome as the new tab and home page, laid out like Fenix's
Homepage.kt (shortcuts, continue, bookmarks, recently visited, private
home), from Places, pinned links and the open tabs.

App menu rows use Fenix's metrics on both versions. MemoryTrim answers
memory pressure the way Fenix's MemoryController does in the background:
only while every window is hidden and the system is short of memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SXjPGasJxD6XRYU1J9jsnW
---
